// P3G.5 ER Ex1 "Using Linked Documents" (external-references.md ER6 steps 1–18, ER6.check;
// ex1-step1.png … ex1-step18.png). The course's public "Linked Document- Piston" and "Linked
// Documents- Project" can't be copied, so the stand-ins are `fixtures/linked_piston_standin.cadrs`
// (Pneumatic Piston: UJoint, Cylinder from Main Sketch Ø15.725, Rod 28, Eye; Piston Assembly)
// and `fixtures/linked_hexapod_standin.cadrs` (the Hexapod with Baseplate <1> fixed and
// Topplate <1>; the Topplate and Baseplate Part Studios), see `cadrs_core::samples::piston`.
// 01 (ER6.1) the documents page, the stand-ins listed; the Piston's menu: Copy… .
// 02 (ER6.1) the Copy dialog, named "Linked Document- Piston".
// 03 (ER6.2) the copy opened; the top bar's Create version: "Create version from Main", V1.
// 04 (ER6.3) the Project copied as "Linked Documents- Project" and opened on the Hexapod: the
//    two plates only.
// 04b (ER1.4) Insert → Other documents → "Linked Document- Piston" searched → the document at V1;
//    its Part Studios searched for "Rod": only the Rod part is listed.
// 05 (ER6.4) Insert → Other documents → "Linked Document- Piston" searched → the document at V1
//    → Assemblies: "Piston Assembly" hovered.
// 06 (ER6.4) Piston Assembly picked and placed: it follows the pointer, "Inserted: 1".
// 07 (ER6.5) ✓: "Piston Assembly <1>" with the version icon (its tooltip).
// 08 (ER6.6) Revolute 1 (`linked-ex hexapod-revolute`: the UJoint's bottom-face centre on the
//    first baseplate hole's top edge centre), its dialog opened from Mate Features: "Mate
//    connector of UJoint", "Mate connector of Baseplate".
// 09 (ER6.7) Piston Assembly <1>'s menu: Copy, Update linked document…, Open linked document,
//    Pin reference, … .
// 10 (ER6.7) Copy, then Ctrl+V five times in the graphics area: Piston Assembly <1>–<6>.
// 11 (ER6.8–ER6.10) the other five Revolutes and Fastened 1–6 (the Eyes' top-face centres on
//    the Topplate holes' bottom edges) (`linked-ex hexapod-mates`, the harness's shortcut for
//    the picks): the Hexapod assembled, Mate Features (12).
// 12 (ER6.18, ER6.check V1) all instances, Mass properties: 309 446.876 + 196 349.541 + 6 ·
//    13 956.271 = 589 534.041 mm³, centroid (0, 0, 50.348); Aluminum 6061: 1.592 kg.
// 13 (ER6.11–ER6.12) the Piston document, Pneumatic Piston, Main Sketch edited: Ø15.725 → Ø20.
// 14 (ER6.13) the rod's length: Extrude 3 (the Rod), depth 28 → 75 (the stand-in's rod length is
//    its extrude's depth); the Eye, sketched on the rod's top, follows.
// 15 (ER6.14) Create version V2.
// 16 (ER6.15) back in the Project: the six Piston Assembly rows and the Hexapod tab show the
//    blue badge; the geometry is unchanged.
// 17 (ER6.16) the six rows selected, their menu: Update linked document… hovered.
// 18 (ER6.16) the Reference manager: "Linked Document- Piston V1 ⇒ V2", Update all.
// 19 (ER6.17) updated: longer pistons, the Topplate raised with them (the mates re-solved), the
//    badges gone; all instances' mass: 640 689.203 mm³, centroid (0, 0, 65.964), 1.730 kg.
// 20 (ER6.17) the toolbar's Update all references → Selective update: each row's version
//    graph → V1, Update selected: back to V1.
// 21 (ER6.check) all instances' mass again: 589 534.041 mm³, centroid (0, 0, 50.348).
